Let the shell draw permission prompts.

Chromium's permission bubble hangs off the location bar. A shell that draws
its own browser UI shows no location bar, so the bubble has nothing to anchor
to -- and on a phone the user is meant to see a bottom sheet in the shell's
own language, with "allow once" and "allow while using this site" as separate
answers.

PermissionPrompt::Delegate already has exactly those outcomes -- Accept,
AcceptThisTime, Deny, Dismiss -- so the shell prompt is a thin one: it sends
sitePermissionRequested, waits, and calls the matching method when
sitePermissionDecision comes back. A request Chromium abandons first sends
sitePermissionCancelled so the shell can take its sheet down.

This is a different thing from the existing permissionsRequested event, which
asks the shell for a HarmonyOS application permission after the user has
already agreed. Both still run, in that order.

Requests the shell has no wording for fall through to Chromium's own UI
rather than going unanswered.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1711,6 +1711,8 @@
       "icon_loader_ohos.cc",
       "memory_details_linux.cc",
       "platform_util_ohos.cc",
+      "ui/ohos/shell_permission_prompt_ohos.cc",
+      "ui/ohos/shell_permission_prompt_ohos.h",
     ]
     deps += [
       "//chrome/browser/printing",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/permission_prompt_factory.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/permission_prompt_factory.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/permission_prompt_factory.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/permission_prompt_factory.cc
@@ -289,6 +289,19 @@
     return nullptr;
   }
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // Before anything that reaches for the location bar: where the shell draws
+  // the browser UI there is none, and every bubble below would hang off a
+  // view that is not on screen. Falls through when the shell has no sheet for
+  // this kind of request.
+  if (chrome::ohos::ShellDrawsPermissionPrompts()) {
+    if (std::unique_ptr<permissions::PermissionPrompt> prompt =
+            chrome::ohos::CreateShellPermissionPrompt(web_contents, delegate)) {
+      return prompt;
+    }
+  }
+#endif
+
   if (ShouldIgnorePermissionRequest(web_contents, delegate)) {
     return nullptr;
   }
